--- !u!114 &204703449
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 204703447}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a11dd23e08e5cb942a6a6b4da8d43711, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TEXDrawRuntime::TexDrawLib.TEXDraw
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_Alignment: {x: 0.5, y: 0.5}
  m_Text: "That\u2019s Correct!\n\nThe rune stones were A, A, and C. Since order
    matters, each different arrangement forms a new result. This is still called
    a permutation but because two of the letters are the same, some arrangements
    are identical. These are called distinct permutations.\n\nLet\u2019s list them:\n\nAAC,
    ACA, CAA\n\nEven though there are 3 letters, swapping the two A\u2019s does not
    create a new arrangement because they are identical.\n\nTo calculate the number
    of distinct permutations, we use:\n\n\\; \\frac{3!}{2!}\n\nWe divide by 2! because
    there are two identical A\u2019s.\n\n\\frac{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}{2 \\times
    1} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\n\nThe three rune stones (A, A, C) have 3 distinct permutations."
  m_Size: 6
  m_ScrollArea:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 0
    y: 0
    width: 0
    height: 0
  m_Padding:
    left: 5
    right: 5
    top: 2
    bottom: 2
  m_Overflow: 0
